{"name":"Goddess of Dawn","hex":"#904c6f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"goddess","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female deity.","An incredibly beautiful, gorgeous, sexy, attractive woman honored and adored for her beauty or of superior charm and intelligence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goddess"},{"term":"dawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To begin to brighten with daylight.","To start to appear or become obvious."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The morning twilight period immediately before sunrise.","The rising of the sun."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fire Emblem: Radiant Dawn","blocks":[{"text":"Fire Emblem: Radiant Dawn is a tactical role-playing game developed by Intelligent Systems and published by Nintendo for the Wii home console. It is the tenth entry in the Fire Emblem series, and acts as a direct sequel to the 2005 GameCube title Fire Emblem: Path of Radiance. It was released in 2007 in Japan and North America, and 2008 in Europe and Australia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d4/Fire_Emblem_Radiant_Dawn_Box_Art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_Emblem%3A_Radiant_Dawn","wikidata":"Q2322497"},{"title":"Dawn deities","blocks":[{"text":"A dawn deity is a deity in a polytheistic religious tradition who is in some sense associated with the dawn. These deities show some relation with the morning, the beginning of the day, and, in some cases, become syncretized with similar solar deities."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn_deities","wikidata":"Q5242541"},{"title":"Goddess","blocks":[{"text":"A goddess is a female deity. In some faiths, a sacred female figure holds a central place in religious prayer and worship. For example, Shaktism, holds that the ultimate deity, the source of all reality, is Supreme Goddess (Mahamaya) and in some forms of Tantric Shaivism, the pair of Shiva and Shakti are the ultimate principle. Meanwhile, in Vajrayana Buddhism, ultimate reality is often seen as being composed of two principles depicted as two deities in union symbolising the non-duality of the two principles of perfect wisdom (female) and skillful compassion (male). A single figure in a monotheistic faith that is female may be identified simply as god because of no need to differentiate by gender or with a diminutive. An experiment to determine the effect of psychedelics on subjects composed of leaders from diverse religious groups revealed a general experience that the divine which the subjects encountered was feminine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Queen_Nefertari_being_led_by_Isis_MET_DP167142.jpg/330px-Queen_Nefertari_being_led_by_Isis_MET_DP167142.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goddess","wikidata":"Q205985"},{"title":"Dawn","blocks":[{"text":"Dawn is the time that marks the beginning of twilight before sunrise. It is recognized by the appearance of indirect daylight being scattered in Earth's atmosphere, when the centre of the Sun's disc has reached 18° below the observer's horizon. This morning twilight period will last until sunrise, when direct daylight outshines the diffused light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Desert_Dawn.jpg/330px-Desert_Dawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn","wikidata":"Q11326182"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8d/FE_Radiant_Dawn_screenshot.jpg/330px-FE_Radiant_Dawn_screenshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8d/FE_Radiant_Dawn_screenshot.jpg/330px-FE_Radiant_Dawn_screenshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A battle in Radiant Dawn","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFE_Radiant_Dawn_screenshot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Ceres_statue.jpg/330px-Ceres_statue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Ceres_statue.jpg/330px-Ceres_statue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Statue of an unknown woman as Ceres, Roman goddess of agriculture and motherly relationships","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeres_statue.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Freia_Gestures_to_Hyndla_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg/500px-Freia_Gestures_to_Hyndla_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Freia_Gestures_to_Hyndla_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg/500px-Freia_Gestures_to_Hyndla_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The goddess Freyja is nuzzled by the boar Hildisvíni while gesturing to Hyndla (1895) by Lorenz Frølich.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFreia_Gestures_to_Hyndla_by_Fr%C3%B8lich.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Toci_and_Xochiquetzal%2C_Two_Aztec_Goddesses_WDL6731.png/500px-Toci_and_Xochiquetzal%2C_Two_Aztec_Goddesses_WDL6731.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Toci_and_Xochiquetzal%2C_Two_Aztec_Goddesses_WDL6731.png/1280px-Toci_and_Xochiquetzal%2C_Two_Aztec_Goddesses_WDL6731.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Toci_and_Xochiquetzal%2C_Two_Aztec_Goddesse